Document
  Body
    Paragraph
      Text "Markdown began as a way to write for the web without writing HTML. It was never\ngiven a grammar, only a description and a script, and every tool since has had\nto decide for itself what the description meant."
    Paragraph
      Text "That is *why* two tools can disagree about the same file. One reads an indented\nline as code; another reads it as the end of a list. Neither is wrong, because\nnothing says which is right."
    Paragraph
      Text "> A format with no grammar is a format with as many grammars as it has readers."
    Paragraph
      Text "The rest of this essay is about living with that."
